 in this  track that are near the ad a gene so I'm  going to use the slider to slide back to  the zoomed out position here and when  the display updates in this view here  I've just highlighted for you here in  red the position of the ad a gene and  down here are those three calls that our  collaborator gave us and down here at  the bottom now is that NHGRI gos catalog  track and you can see that there are  actually some hits in this track that  are just down stream of the adn gene so  blowing this up we can take a better  look at the content of this particular  track in this track both the scatterplot  above these bins and the business  themselves reflect individual p-values  so both the color and the dots location  correspond to the p-value and we're also  getting here the count of reported  associations for that snip so if we  hover our mouse over the bin that has  the top hit right here we get a tooltip  that opens up and we see that this  particular snip which I've highlighted  here in red is a result from the GYC  catalog and it reflects an association  with ulcerative colitis and there's a  link down here to cut med so we can get  more information so by looking at the  content in this tooltip and this track  we're able to tell our collaborator that  they might want to follow up on this  particular information to further  evaluate a punitive link between a da  and irritable bowel disease so while  this concludes the very  analyses that we're going to do today in  our webinar I also want to point out  that there are other browser features  that you might find useful in your  analyses first I want to emphasize that  you can share your configure display  with your colleagues by clicking on this  share this page link at the top right a  variation viewer secondly you can save  your track configurations in the display  to your my NCBI account using the my  NCBI track collections option it's here  underneath the tracks menu lastly by  clicking on the Tools menu you c